("h3", "Displacement and the reactivity idea"),
("p", "A more reactive metal pushes a less reactive metal out of its salt solution. Iron nail in blue copper sulphate solution: the solution fades towards green and a brown deposit of copper forms. Zinc displaces copper, and lead displaces copper from copper chloride, but copper cannot displace iron."),
