("p", "When metals are slowly eaten away by air, moisture or chemicals the process is **corrosion**. The reddish-brown coating on iron is **rust** (hydrated iron oxide); the black coating on silver is silver sulphide; the green coating on copper is basic copper carbonate. Rusting needs **both air (oxygen) and water**."),
("ul", ["Prevention: painting, oiling, greasing, galvanising (zinc coating), chrome plating, anodising, making alloys.", "Corrosion damages bridges, ships, railings and car bodies, costing huge sums every year."]),
